# Agent debug — identities and message lookup

Mirrored for Antigravity: [`.agents/rules/agent-debug.md`](../../.agents/rules/agent-debug.md)

## Two identities — do not mix them up

| Use | iid | alien_id | When |
|-----|-----|----------|------|
| **Automated tests** | **33000** | `automated-tester` | MCP prompt/tool tests, seeds, fixtures — see `automated-tester.mdc` |
| **Your real account (Chito)** | **99000** | `chito` | Inspecting production-like chats, billing, consumption you logged in the app |

Default **message / trace inspection** for “what did I see in the app?” → **`owner_iid = 99000`**.

Default **automated regression** → **`owner_iid = 33000`**.

## Inspecting a turn

Prefer `msg_get` / `trace_get` / `msg_find` / `log_tail` on the `c35` MCP. Fall back to `yb` SQL on `ai.chat_msg` and `ai.log` (`database=c35`).

1. Message id → that row plus the same `req_id` in `ai.log`.
2. `req_id` → `chat_msg` + `log`.
3. Text only to discover ids → `owner_iid = 99000`, `content ILIKE`, newest first.

`prompt_run` / `prompt_compose` default to **33000**. Pass **99000** for Chito's data. Device tools default to **99000**; do not drive another owner's devices (`device-control-chito.mdc`).
